# Winter, Cursed Rider: "Exhaust - {2}{U}{B}, {T}, Exile X artifact cards from your graveyard: Each other nonartifact creature gets -X/-X
# until end of turn." X is announced as the ability is activated, with no {X} in its cost (CR 107.3a, 602.2b), and the cost exiles that many
# cards (CR 602.2b, 601.2h).
# Turn 1 Bot1 casts Winter and sacrifices three Mishra's Baubles (three artifact cards in its graveyard). Turn 2 Bot2 casts a Wall of
# Wood (0/3) and a Steel Wall (0/4, an artifact) and sacrifices a Bauble of its own. Turn 3 Bot1 casts its own Kraken Hatchling (0/4) and
# a Dark Ritual (a nonartifact card, now in its graveyard too).
# The cost is refused for want of {U} while only an untapped Mox Emerald stands beside the {B}{B}{B} in the pool. Then X = 2 is announced,
# X = 4 is refused (three artifact cards), the Ritual is not a card the cost takes, and the pool ({B}{B}{B} and the Island's {U}) pays
# {2}{U}{B} exactly: two of the three Baubles are exiled, the third stays, and Bot2's Bauble stays too ("your graveyard").
# Bot2's Wall of Wood and the Hatchling become -2/1 and -2/2 (each creature, both players'), Steel Wall (an artifact) and Winter itself
# (other) are untouched. On turn 4 they are 0/3 and 0/4 again. On turn 5 the ability, used once, cannot be activated again (exhaust).

